  "notes": "Subdivided icosphere (80 triangles, 42 vertices) with a deterministic sine displacement of +-6%, underside flattened only at 93% of the radius so it still reads as a water-worn pebble; fit_bounds pins 50 x 42 x 35 mm.  One closed shell, no boolean, no extra triangles.  Chip: every face whose centre points within the CHIP_DIRECTION cap is collected and all of its vertices are clamped onto one plane 0.020 radii below the cap peak, so the cap becomes a single flat facet (flint slot).  Crack: every vertex within 0.20 of the CRACK_NORMAL plane is pulled inward by up to 9%, and the faces within 0.16 of it take the wood_dark slot.",
